      "value": "@{5e44a1bd0c91c2477a8b8acb|full_name}: The additive layer is for small adjustments, like the breathing animation in the example additive controller. Even if you set your layers inside to override they are forced to additive by the SDK, meaning they get added on top of your locomotion animations. \nIf you try to put an animation there that's anything other than subtle, you'll get weird results. See the image below, which is what my working desktop arm control pose looks like when it's in the additive layer. The arm is supposed to be straight. \nI do wish it worked for this because it would be an easy enough workaround, considering most people usually have nothing else in there. But sadly it's neither the right place nor a viable workaround for this kind of animation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
